<title>ISRAEL: RESEARCH ALERT-Teva earnings revised.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT-Teva earnings revised.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1997-04-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lehman Brothers said on Sunday it had lowered its 1997 earnings per share (EPS) estimte of Teva Pharmaceutical Industries to $2.75 from $3.00.</p>
<p>The investment house said the revision reflected what it believed would be a lower profit contribution of $0.55 per share by Teva's multiple sclerosis drug Copaxone.</p>
<p>Lehman said that without the benefit of a full year's worth of Copaxone sales in the United States and upfront promotional spending, it felt the previous Copaxone estimate of 1.00 dollar per share might be too aggressive.</p>
<p>The drug was officially launched in early April.</p>
<p>Lehman has left unchanged its 1998 EPS estimate at $4.90.</p>
<p>- Tel Aviv newsroom 537-2211</p>
</text>
